replace("await androidChooseStartup(initial.startup||{});", "await androidChooseStartup(initial.startup||{});DesktopHost.call('mediaSettings',{voice:S.listen.voice,rate:S.listen.rate,rules:S.listen.rules}).catch(console.warn);DesktopHost.call('mediaState').catch(console.warn);")
replace('const HELP_TOPICS=[', "const HELP_TOPICS=[\n {id:'android-auto',category:'listening',title:'Android Auto and background narration',summary:'Browse books and listen to chapters in your car.',keywords:'car android auto background screen off notification bluetooth',body:`<p>Open and save a project on the phone before driving. Android Auto shows NovelWeaver as a media app, with books and chapters. Select a chapter to start narration. Play/pause and previous/next chapter are available in the car and playback notification. Narration continues with the screen off, using saved narrator/dialogue presets and pronunciation rules.</p><p>When the editor is closed, the service reads the last project from its actual file. Cloud files must be accessible; download local voices and keep project files available offline before driving. A missing file is reported in the car; reopen it on the phone while parked. Editing stays on the phone.</p><p>For a directly installed APK, open Android Auto settings, tap Version information ten times, accept developer mode, then open the three-dot menu → Developer settings → Unknown sources. Reconnect Android Auto and check Customize launcher. This enables testing; it does not grant Google Play certification.</p><p>Pausing preserves the current spoken segment while the service lives. Restarting the service resumes from the last paragraph, not an exact audio timestamp. Narration pauses for audio interruptions or disconnected headphones. Offline playback needs local TTS voices; online voices require network access.</p>`},")

